(4738762, 683852, 68035, '<td valign="top">Oh my word, if this is taken by who I think it is taken then all I can say is that you saved the best iceberg shot till last.<br/> <br/>This is absolutely wondrous, such simple beauty and majesty, incredible curves on the berg and I love the three colours, the white of the iceberg, the aquamarine of the berg below the water level and the darkness of the water that surrounds it (which bizarrely looks even colder than the iceberg itself)<br/> <br/>Such strong lines, such an incredible photograph.  <br/> <br/>The highest compliment I can pay this shot is that I would love to have it framed in my house, and if it was taken by who I think it might have been taken by it would be an honour if you would sign a copy of the print when you come to the UK before I had it framed (My only doubt is that I saw the person I thought it was saying they were scoring under a six in the forums which if true would be a travesty)<br/> <br/>One of my two favourite ever shots on DPC<br/> <br/>10 and straight to favourites</td>', 'Oh my word, if this is taken by who I think it is taken then all I can say is that you saved the best iceberg shot till last. This is absolutely wondrous, such simple beauty and majesty, incredible curves on the berg and I love the three colours, the white of the iceberg, the aquamarine of the berg below the water level and the darkness of the water that surrounds it (which bizarrely looks even colder than the iceberg itself) Such strong lines, such an incredible photograph.   The highest compliment I can pay this shot is that I would love to have it framed in my house, and if it was taken by who I think it might have been taken by it would be an honour if you would sign a copy of the print when you come to the UK before I had it framed (My only doubt is that I saw the person I thought it was saying they were scoring under a six in the forums which if true would be a travesty) One of my two favourite ever shots on DPC 10 and straight to favourites', '2008-06-01 13:41:11.000000', NULL, 1),
