(4756548, 682309, 89940, '<td valign="top">Big Sur right? I''ve been meaning to go here all year and just haven''t found the time. Beautiful shot.</td>', 'Big Sur right? I''ve been meaning to go here all year and just haven''t found the time. Beautiful shot.', '2008-06-07 19:47:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756551, 677178, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - Beautiful.  Very good concept.  Excellent title.  Fairly minor, but ''Be Different'' - all in title case would be better in my opinion.  Like to have seen the ''different one'' ''pop'' more, somehow (maybe even by a variation in crop, although I <i>do</i> like your framing, crop and composition).  Maybe also cloning out the tip of a bud poking over the top as well, but again, fairly minor.</td>', '8 - Beautiful.  Very good concept.  Excellent title.  Fairly minor, but ''Be Different'' - all in title case would be better in my opinion.  Like to have seen the ''different one'' ''pop'' more, somehow (maybe even by a variation in crop, although I do like your framing, crop and composition).  Maybe also cloning out the tip of a bud poking over the top as well, but again, fairly minor.', '2008-06-07 19:49:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756552, 678848, 3746, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot.. should finish very high.. maybe ribbon? 10</td>', 'Awesome shot.. should finish very high.. maybe ribbon? 10', '2008-06-07 19:49:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756555, 683985, 89940, '<td valign="top">great concept and superb lighting. I''m going to have to try this.</td>', 'great concept and superb lighting. I''m going to have to try this.', '2008-06-07 19:50:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756561, 682881, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Looks like the details lost at this size are likely there wall sized and this would make an excellent ''wall sized'', especially with the right framing.  I like that this is different by being (seemingly) deliberately cold, isolated and ''lackluster''.  After looking at this a while, the ponting/deck dominates more and leads the eye ''out'' of the frame to the right, yet the distant sloping of the landscape and edge of the lake are not quite strong enough to counter-balance that bringing the balance/eye back to the left of frame, if that makes sense.  Perhaps tweaking that ''somehow'' may have made this even stronger, that coupled with perhaps a more refined crop on the left where there is ''half'' a hill/mountain in the frame.</td>', '7 - Looks like the details lost at this size are likely there wall sized and this would make an excellent ''wall sized'', especially with the right framing.  I like that this is different by being (seemingly) deliberately cold, isolated and ''lackluster''.  After looking at this a while, the ponting/deck dominates more and leads the eye ''out'' of the frame to the right, yet the distant sloping of the landscape and edge of the lake are not quite strong enough to counter-balance that bringing the balance/eye back to the left of frame, if that makes sense.  Perhaps tweaking that ''somehow'' may have made this even stronger, that coupled with perhaps a more refined crop on the left where there is ''half'' a hill/mountain in the frame.', '2008-06-07 19:55:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756573, 677477, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - ''Aww'', only a baby.  Wish he/she dominated the frame more, a variation in crop likely have given this extra, in my opinion.</td>', '6 - ''Aww'', only a baby.  Wish he/she dominated the frame more, a variation in crop likely have given this extra, in my opinion.', '2008-06-07 20:01:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756589, 684060, 39850, '<td valign="top">6 - Very good bold colors of the buildings (and a good assortment and example of architecture there as well) - the way they ''pop'' against the dark sky and those fluffy white clouds is good.  The sign on the bank detracts, but fairly minor.  Your title almost works against the image, in my opinion - because I then look for the cathedral and find it is such a small part of the image and not ''showcased'' very well from this perspective, if that makes sense.</td>', '6 - Very good bold colors of the buildings (and a good assortment and example of architecture there as well) - the way they ''pop'' against the dark sky and those fluffy white clouds is good.  The sign on the bank detracts, but fairly minor.  Your title almost works against the image, in my opinion - because I then look for the cathedral and find it is such a small part of the image and not ''showcased'' very well from this perspective, if that makes sense.', '2008-06-07 20:08:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756597, 683411, 39850, '<td valign="top">5 - Don''t mind the concept (seemingly infrared, etc) but wonder whether this 720 might have packed more punch.  Perhaps a more refined crop too, although I like the composition.  As for your title - even in ''grayscale'', this doesn''t look like such a bad place to ''have a life'', but then, of course, that''s just my opinion.</td>', '5 - Don''t mind the concept (seemingly infrared, etc) but wonder whether this 720 might have packed more punch.  Perhaps a more refined crop too, although I like the composition.  As for your title - even in ''grayscale'', this doesn''t look like such a bad place to ''have a life'', but then, of course, that''s just my opinion.', '2008-06-07 20:10:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756628, 681609, 89940, '<td valign="top">Cute kitty. Is not the sharpest photo and there appears to be quite a bit of noise.</td>', 'Cute kitty. Is not the sharpest photo and there appears to be quite a bit of noise.', '2008-06-07 20:28:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756632, 681102, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Beautiful capture.  My two biggest ''nit-picks'' are the silhouette on the rider and that this isn''t 720.  The ''dust'' sets the mood for the whole image.</td>', '7 - Beautiful capture.  My two biggest ''nit-picks'' are the silhouette on the rider and that this isn''t 720.  The ''dust'' sets the mood for the whole image.', '2008-06-07 20:33:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756636, 676992, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Good image.  At first the fact that she isn''t (or seemingly) looking straight into the camera distracted me, but then.. I think that actually makes this more unusual and takes it to another level.  Perhaps a crop variation may have made this image even stronger, not sure.</td>', '7 - Good image.  At first the fact that she isn''t (or seemingly) looking straight into the camera distracted me, but then.. I think that actually makes this more unusual and takes it to another level.  Perhaps a crop variation may have made this image even stronger, not sure.', '2008-06-07 20:37:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756651, 682401, 89940, '<td valign="top">I think this would look better cropped more. My eye was drawn to the tree initially and then to the Egret. So perhaps cutting out most of the tree would cause the Egret to be the clear subject</td>', 'I think this would look better cropped more. My eye was drawn to the tree initially and then to the Egret. So perhaps cutting out most of the tree would cause the Egret to be the clear subject', '2008-06-07 20:55:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756655, 683339, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - This image grows on you the more you look at it.  Excellent composition.</td>', '7 - This image grows on you the more you look at it.  Excellent composition.', '2008-06-07 20:57:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756657, 684209, 89940, '<td valign="top">This it the 3rd photo I''ve seen of the Cadillac farm this week. Weird that it keeps turning up. I like the sky and city lights in the background. Wish the cars were a little more brightly lit.</td>', 'This it the 3rd photo I''ve seen of the Cadillac farm this week. Weird that it keeps turning up. I like the sky and city lights in the background. Wish the cars were a little more brightly lit.', '2008-06-07 20:58:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756671, 684294, 39850, '<td valign="top">1 - Don''t understand the look on her face.  Don''t understand why you would want to take a ''practical, everyday (albeit rarely seen) happening'' and try to turn it into ''art'' (this is hardly photojournalistic).  Don''t understand your message, if you have one.  Not sure that I care to try.  I may look pc to see if you ''made notes'', but otherwise, this is probably just another ''shock factor'' image that portrays things that some people see every day - again, in a practical sense.  The death of an animal shouldn''t be ''showcased''.  It is what it is and serves a purpose.  Yes, all my opinion - but you put this out there.  I am not ''shocked'' by it, nor disturbed - only by your mindset in conceptualizing and capturing such an image.  The photograph itself is quite well done and processed - but that doesn''t change the fact that this is a staged image that twists something.........  for what purpose, what.  And your title only cements my translation of the image.  Normally I''d give an extra point for creativity, but not with this.  If I get no other message across (yes mine, not yours - hence the ''comment box''), this is disrespectful to the animal.</td>', '1 - Don''t understand the look on her face.  Don''t understand why you would want to take a ''practical, everyday (albeit rarely seen) happening'' and try to turn it into ''art'' (this is hardly photojournalistic).  Don''t understand your message, if you have one.  Not sure that I care to try.  I may look pc to see if you ''made notes'', but otherwise, this is probably just another ''shock factor'' image that portrays things that some people see every day - again, in a practical sense.  The death of an animal shouldn''t be ''showcased''.  It is what it is and serves a purpose.  Yes, all my opinion - but you put this out there.  I am not ''shocked'' by it, nor disturbed - only by your mindset in conceptualizing and capturing such an image.  The photograph itself is quite well done and processed - but that doesn''t change the fact that this is a staged image that twists something.........  for what purpose, what.  And your title only cements my translation of the image.  Normally I''d give an extra point for creativity, but not with this.  If I get no other message across (yes mine, not yours - hence the ''comment box''), this is disrespectful to the animal.', '2008-06-07 21:21:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(4756675, 675972, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Make a nice ''wall sized''.</td>', '7 - Make a nice ''wall sized''.', '2008-06-07 21:26:21.000000', NULL, 1),
