(4757286, 683852, 68035, '<td valign="top">Well you know my views on this shot!  I am glad that it rallied somewhat in the voting although at MINIMUM this was a top ten for me<br/> <br/>Utter exquisite beauty</td>', 'Well you know my views on this shot!  I am glad that it rallied somewhat in the voting although at MINIMUM this was a top ten for me Utter exquisite beauty', '2008-06-08 04:17:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757287, 683058, 30982, '<td valign="top">Underrated - I really like the processing.  She looks like a young Princess Di and oh so serious!</td>', 'Underrated - I really like the processing.  She looks like a young Princess Di and oh so serious!', '2008-06-08 04:20:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757290, 681207, 68035, '<td valign="top">Great story (in the interesting rather than positive sense of the word) and a great image (as in the positive sense of the word).  There were a couple of foxes in the free study and I thought that this stood out a mile.  Super sharpness and wonderful rich colours.  Thanks for explaining about the background, I had wondered but understand that it was circumstance and bot chice <br/> <br/>Great finish in a FS - congratulations</td>', 'Great story (in the interesting rather than positive sense of the word) and a great image (as in the positive sense of the word).  There were a couple of foxes in the free study and I thought that this stood out a mile.  Super sharpness and wonderful rich colours.  Thanks for explaining about the background, I had wondered but understand that it was circumstance and bot chice  Great finish in a FS - congratulations', '2008-06-08 04:22:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757292, 684097, 30982, '<td valign="top">Woefully underappreciated.  This is really a very good shot.</td>', 'Woefully underappreciated.  This is really a very good shot.', '2008-06-08 04:23:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757293, 682445, 68035, '<td valign="top">Well you know that I think it is a beautiful shot and I love the PP.<br/> <br/>Should have scored higher in my opinion, I love it</td>', 'Well you know that I think it is a beautiful shot and I love the PP. Should have scored higher in my opinion, I love it', '2008-06-08 04:24:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757294, 683729, 88523, '<td valign="top">Nice one nick! Surreal and quirky...</td>', 'Nice one nick! Surreal and quirky...', '2008-06-08 04:25:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757295, 684192, 30982, '<td valign="top">Really nicely done to bring out the detail on the uppermost part of that ceiliing!  (I was there earlier this year and have lots of shots of the place - it''s gorgeous, isn''t it?)</td>', 'Really nicely done to bring out the detail on the uppermost part of that ceiliing!  (I was there earlier this year and have lots of shots of the place - it''s gorgeous, isn''t it?)', '2008-06-08 04:25:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757299, 683722, 30982, '<td valign="top">I really like this composition for this showy bird - a nice change from the usual shot.</td>', 'I really like this composition for this showy bird - a nice change from the usual shot.', '2008-06-08 04:29:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757306, 682447, 68035, '<td valign="top">Peter<br/> <br/>Well first of all you need to take this out of the free study context and ask yourself is it a great landscape and the answer is without a doubt.<br/> <br/>Beautifully composed, strong leading lines, visually very aestetic nice reflection etc. <br/> <br/>I guess my one issue may be that it does not uniformedly have the pinpoint infinite sharpness that some landscapes do.  Let me emphasise that this is a very small point but now taking it into a DPC context then the slightest flaw in a FS will be pounced upon.  However lets also be honest and say that that is a pretty healthy looking scoring graph that you have there, no 1s or 2s and a 6 average (which is incidentally what I scored it)<br/> <br/>One thought, I notice that you tonemapped this and I just wonder whether in this instance that was maybe a step to far and you could have stayed with ''traditional'' techniques<br/> <br/>Let me tell you Peter if I had taken this shot I would be very proud, I do think it is strong and striking but perhaps without the wow factor that will make it top 20<br/> <br/>Nice job</td>', 'Peter Well first of all you need to take this out of the free study context and ask yourself is it a great landscape and the answer is without a doubt. Beautifully composed, strong leading lines, visually very aestetic nice reflection etc.  I guess my one issue may be that it does not uniformedly have the pinpoint infinite sharpness that some landscapes do.  Let me emphasise that this is a very small point but now taking it into a DPC context then the slightest flaw in a FS will be pounced upon.  However lets also be honest and say that that is a pretty healthy looking scoring graph that you have there, no 1s or 2s and a 6 average (which is incidentally what I scored it) One thought, I notice that you tonemapped this and I just wonder whether in this instance that was maybe a step to far and you could have stayed with ''traditional'' techniques Let me tell you Peter if I had taken this shot I would be very proud, I do think it is strong and striking but perhaps without the wow factor that will make it top 20 Nice job', '2008-06-08 04:36:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757310, 679827, 68035, '<td valign="top">Gosh I realise that I should have recognised the jumper from your earlier entry.<br/> <br/>Great job and I am surprised that it did not score higher<br/> <br/>Lovely imagery</td>', 'Gosh I realise that I should have recognised the jumper from your earlier entry. Great job and I am surprised that it did not score higher Lovely imagery', '2008-06-08 04:39:06.000000', NULL, 0),
