(4757738, 683985, 19936, '<td valign="top">Very creative.  Love the soft light and action of the bubbles.</td>', 'Very creative.  Love the soft light and action of the bubbles.', '2008-06-08 12:58:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757742, 681760, 5728, '<td valign="top">Giving a very rare appearance as critique club member here. Going from the comments there wasn''t too much helpful there for you, mainly comments about how cute the Gosling is or how cool the water drops are. Unfortunately, you were wrong in your prediction of a personal best score, but you were right in it being one of your best shots. You hit the exposure right on the button here and even with an f9 aperture you still managed to get a decent blur on the back of the Gosling and the water in the background. I bet you were chuffed when you saw the result on the screen, probably even before when you saw it on the camera display. The Gosling''s reflections are cool, I think it kicks this image even more than the water drops do. I find what harmed your score in general is the crop. I find it a little too tight and would maybe have given the Gosling a little more freedom as here I get the feeling it is somewhat trapped in the framing you chose. Including the full reflection in the image could have been advantageous also.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-08 12:02:46.</i></td>', 'Giving a very rare appearance as critique club member here. Going from the comments there wasn''t too much helpful there for you, mainly comments about how cute the Gosling is or how cool the water drops are. Unfortunately, you were wrong in your prediction of a personal best score, but you were right in it being one of your best shots. You hit the exposure right on the button here and even with an f9 aperture you still managed to get a decent blur on the back of the Gosling and the water in the background. I bet you were chuffed when you saw the result on the screen, probably even before when you saw it on the camera display. The Gosling''s reflections are cool, I think it kicks this image even more than the water drops do. I find what harmed your score in general is the crop. I find it a little too tight and would maybe have given the Gosling a little more freedom as here I get the feeling it is somewhat trapped in the framing you chose. Including the full reflection in the image could have been advantageous also.', '2008-06-08 13:01:19.000000', '2008-06-08 13:02:46.000000', 0),
(4757744, 681567, 68586, '<td valign="top">Beautiful detail on the back of his head - not easy when it is just black fur - but you''ve really got it to ''pop''. Great sense of depth to the shot as well.</td>', 'Beautiful detail on the back of his head - not easy when it is just black fur - but you''ve really got it to ''pop''. Great sense of depth to the shot as well.', '2008-06-08 13:01:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757745, 681678, 80058, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hotpasta:</b></div><hr/><i> I wish this was at least in the top 10...I love this! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I back you up!! =)</td>', 'Originally posted by hotpasta: I wish this was at least in the top 10...I love this!  I back you up!! =)', '2008-06-08 13:02:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757748, 684313, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> A bit strong on the processing for some, I''m sure, but you really did create another world out of a flower shot - very cool! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I named the photo as I did because it really reminded me of the swirling cloud of demons at the end of <a href="//www.inetres.com/gp/anime/fantasia/index3.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">"Night on Bald Mountain"</a> as depicted in Disney''s <b>Fantasia</b>.</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: A bit strong on the processing for some, I''m sure, but you really did create another world out of a flower shot - very cool!  I named the photo as I did because it really reminded me of the swirling cloud of demons at the end of "Night on Bald Mountain" as depicted in Disney''s Fantasia.', '2008-06-08 13:03:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757753, 684247, 28532, '<td valign="top">Sweet!! Congrats on the ribbon!!!</td>', 'Sweet!! Congrats on the ribbon!!!', '2008-06-08 13:05:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757772, 681513, 91496, '<td valign="top">This angle rocks.  The textures in the lower part of the boat are really nice and the way everything else reaches and points skyward (toward both light and dark sky) is very alluring.</td>', 'This angle rocks.  The textures in the lower part of the boat are really nice and the way everything else reaches and points skyward (toward both light and dark sky) is very alluring.', '2008-06-08 13:17:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757778, 683985, 42013, '<td valign="top">Congrats, well thought out and executed--you''re a master of light.</td>', 'Congrats, well thought out and executed--you''re a master of light.', '2008-06-08 13:23:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757779, 682797, 30982, '<td valign="top">A sub-5??  Holy freakin'' cow.  You do know it''s WAY WAY better than that, right?  This is magical.  A wonderfully composed, edited, and presented image with a lovely story to tell.</td>', 'A sub-5??  Holy freakin'' cow.  You do know it''s WAY WAY better than that, right?  This is magical.  A wonderfully composed, edited, and presented image with a lovely story to tell.', '2008-06-08 13:23:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757790, 682797, 42100, '<td valign="top">I''ll just quote Deb, because she is 100% correct!!!<br/> <br/>...and Pasta...you don''t remember when you got your very first pocket knife and all the hours spent carving points onto sticks!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> A sub-5??  Holy freakin'' cow.  You do know it''s WAY WAY better than that, right?  This is magical.  A wonderfully composed, edited, and presented image with a lovely story to tell. </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-08 12:32:32.</i></td>', 'I''ll just quote Deb, because she is 100% correct!!! ...and Pasta...you don''t remember when you got your very first pocket knife and all the hours spent carving points onto sticks! Originally posted by Melethia: A sub-5??  Holy freakin'' cow.  You do know it''s WAY WAY better than that, right?  This is magical.  A wonderfully composed, edited, and presented image with a lovely story to tell. ', '2008-06-08 13:29:17.000000', '2008-06-08 13:32:32.000000', 0),
(4757796, 681279, 67697, '<td valign="top">Interesting editing and quite a beautiful scene!  There''s so much to see here.  Love the clouds and the birds in the background too.</td>', 'Interesting editing and quite a beautiful scene!  There''s so much to see here.  Love the clouds and the birds in the background too.', '2008-06-08 13:31:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757800, 684267, 51538, '<td valign="top">There''s an art to getting rich deep darkness into a digital photo.  You certainly captured those tones in this one.  Nice view.</td>', 'There''s an art to getting rich deep darkness into a digital photo.  You certainly captured those tones in this one.  Nice view.', '2008-06-08 13:32:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757806, 683961, 67697, '<td valign="top">I thought this had kind of looked familiar.  I love the blue tones.  The silky reflection is gorgeous too.  Congrats on 9th place!</td>', 'I thought this had kind of looked familiar.  I love the blue tones.  The silky reflection is gorgeous too.  Congrats on 9th place!', '2008-06-08 13:36:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757807, 682644, 44877, '<td valign="top">I cannot even believe this scored so low. It''s absolutely lovely and beautifully artistic. Gorgeous work - please continue.</td>', 'I cannot even believe this scored so low. It''s absolutely lovely and beautifully artistic. Gorgeous work - please continue.', '2008-06-08 13:36:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757836, 684247, 55892, '<td valign="top">Stunning! Well deserved ribbon. Congrats.</td>', 'Stunning! Well deserved ribbon. Congrats.', '2008-06-08 13:48:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4757842, 675840, 44877, '<td valign="top">Very good, Juliet. I''d love to see this in a huge version on a wall. The web doesn''t do it justice, nor does the stupid score.</td>', 'Very good, Juliet. I''d love to see this in a huge version on a wall. The web doesn''t do it justice, nor does the stupid score.', '2008-06-08 13:49:47.000000', NULL, 0),
