(4760221, 678848, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Magno:</b></div><hr/><i> My initial thoughts were right! Congratulations on your blue - much deserved. I just wish you weren''t as good as you are, because it sure as hell makes me depressed knowing what you can do in pp, and knowing how inadequate I am at it too!!! lol.<br/> <br/>I''m going to start a petition, to get you to reveal your secrets and give us a tutorial. All in favour say ''I''. Lol. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I added my editing steps. It''s probably not exactly what you''re looking for. If I have time I''ll see if I can write something a bit more indepth. In the past I have posted how I do things. If you look in my <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/portfolio.php?USER_ID=41337&amp;collection_id=26309" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">photo composite</a> gallery there are some there that explains in more indepth the steps including some threads about it. Nothing I''ve done here is any different than what I''ve been doing before.</td>', 'Originally posted by Magno: My initial thoughts were right! Congratulations on your blue - much deserved. I just wish you weren''t as good as you are, because it sure as hell makes me depressed knowing what you can do in pp, and knowing how inadequate I am at it too!!! lol. I''m going to start a petition, to get you to reveal your secrets and give us a tutorial. All in favour say ''I''. Lol.   I added my editing steps. It''s probably not exactly what you''re looking for. If I have time I''ll see if I can write something a bit more indepth. In the past I have posted how I do things. If you look in my photo composite gallery there are some there that explains in more indepth the steps including some threads about it. Nothing I''ve done here is any different than what I''ve been doing before.', '2008-06-09 20:20:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760252, 677178, 74979, '<td valign="top">beautiful and creative..did you add that one??<br/> <br/>:)</td>', 'beautiful and creative..did you add that one?? :)', '2008-06-09 20:38:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760329, 681567, 41337, '<td valign="top">This may just be me being pessimistic but I feel voters in general don''t care about stories in photographs especially when accompanied by a title that tries to explain part or all of it. I''m pretty sure had you just showed the dog''s face and gave it some profound or poetic title your score would have fetched a higher score. Lame pun, I know!</td>', 'This may just be me being pessimistic but I feel voters in general don''t care about stories in photographs especially when accompanied by a title that tries to explain part or all of it. I''m pretty sure had you just showed the dog''s face and gave it some profound or poetic title your score would have fetched a higher score. Lame pun, I know!', '2008-06-09 21:07:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760438, 684247, 60805, '<td valign="top">Spectacular! congrats on the red</td>', 'Spectacular! congrats on the red', '2008-06-09 22:14:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760505, 678848, 33361, '<td valign="top">HA - bet you shot this in Lago Vista! FABULOUS image Richard!! Congrats!!</td>', 'HA - bet you shot this in Lago Vista! FABULOUS image Richard!! Congrats!!', '2008-06-09 22:50:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760583, 677462, 33361, '<td valign="top">who cares.. it''s still fabulous!</td>', 'who cares.. it''s still fabulous!', '2008-06-09 23:15:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760590, 677462, 90387, '<td valign="top">I have to say, it''s an awesome image either way.  I''ve got a real soft spot for B&amp;W though, and this one was very nicely converted.  Everything is so smoooooth.  Nice job!</td>', 'I have to say, it''s an awesome image either way.  I''ve got a real soft spot for B&W though, and this one was very nicely converted.  Everything is so smoooooth.  Nice job!', '2008-06-09 23:18:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760633, 682095, 34659, '<td valign="top">I''m so flattered to finish right behind this image...  This is one of my favorites (and few 10s I gave) in this challenge.  Stunning clarity and color.  I''m a sucker for a great bird shot and this certainly qualifies.  Well done.</td>', 'I''m so flattered to finish right behind this image...  This is one of my favorites (and few 10s I gave) in this challenge.  Stunning clarity and color.  I''m a sucker for a great bird shot and this certainly qualifies.  Well done.', '2008-06-09 23:31:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760643, 681207, 34659, '<td valign="top">I scored this a 9 during voting, but have grown to appreciate it even more since. Beautiful tones and lighting.  Very well done.</td>', 'I scored this a 9 during voting, but have grown to appreciate it even more since. Beautiful tones and lighting.  Very well done.', '2008-06-09 23:33:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760647, 682657, 34659, '<td valign="top">The eyes are just amazing in this portrait.  Beautiful image.  Well done and congrats on the top 15 finish.</td>', 'The eyes are just amazing in this portrait.  Beautiful image.  Well done and congrats on the top 15 finish.', '2008-06-09 23:34:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760654, 683556, 34659, '<td valign="top">Oddly enough, one of my best friends just returned from a journey to this very spot (and after her description, I knew it had to be the same place she visited).  The turquoise water is evidently one of its most distinguishing characteristics. Gorgeous representation.  Just the right amount of cotton candy in this classic waterfall shot.  It garnered a 10 from me.  Beautiful.</td>', 'Oddly enough, one of my best friends just returned from a journey to this very spot (and after her description, I knew it had to be the same place she visited).  The turquoise water is evidently one of its most distinguishing characteristics. Gorgeous representation.  Just the right amount of cotton candy in this classic waterfall shot.  It garnered a 10 from me.  Beautiful.', '2008-06-09 23:36:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760660, 683979, 34659, '<td valign="top">This looked so much like one of your masterpieces Les...  Love the work you''ve done here.  The image manages to capture a story and a personality (like no one else but you can do).  Beautiful image.</td>', 'This looked so much like one of your masterpieces Les...  Love the work you''ve done here.  The image manages to capture a story and a personality (like no one else but you can do).  Beautiful image.', '2008-06-09 23:38:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760663, 678727, 34659, '<td valign="top">The light and clarity in this shot are amazing.  It makes me feel like I''m there in a super-real fashion.  Fantastic work.</td>', 'The light and clarity in this shot are amazing.  It makes me feel like I''m there in a super-real fashion.  Fantastic work.', '2008-06-09 23:38:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760666, 681761, 34659, '<td valign="top">The processing here makes the shot unforgettable.  Outstanding work.</td>', 'The processing here makes the shot unforgettable.  Outstanding work.', '2008-06-09 23:39:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760672, 683417, 34659, '<td valign="top">I love this POV and the richness of the tones.  I should have known that it was your work.  This one got a 10 from me and I wouldn''t change a thing.  Simply beautiful.</td>', 'I love this POV and the richness of the tones.  I should have known that it was your work.  This one got a 10 from me and I wouldn''t change a thing.  Simply beautiful.', '2008-06-09 23:40:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760683, 684247, 34659, '<td valign="top">This is one of those shots that when you initially see it you are stunned by the subtlety of the lighting and impact.  Then after viewing it a few times, you find yourself fascinated by the intricacies of the scene.  I grew up with peacocks (albeit they were not albinos) and there are few representations that are superior to this rendering.  Well done and congratulations on your ribbon.</td>', 'This is one of those shots that when you initially see it you are stunned by the subtlety of the lighting and impact.  Then after viewing it a few times, you find yourself fascinated by the intricacies of the scene.  I grew up with peacocks (albeit they were not albinos) and there are few representations that are superior to this rendering.  Well done and congratulations on your ribbon.', '2008-06-09 23:43:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760694, 678848, 34659, '<td valign="top">Dude...  First, the image is fantastic!!!  It blew me away when I saw it during voting.  After seeing your original, you have given me hope for saving some of my images.  Your processing techniques are impeccable and I can''t state enough how much I appreciate the fact that you showed your original.  This is a truly perfect example of how you can process an image to convey your own personal vision.  Expertly accomplished and definitely worthy of the blue ribbon.  Congratulations!</td>', 'Dude...  First, the image is fantastic!!!  It blew me away when I saw it during voting.  After seeing your original, you have given me hope for saving some of my images.  Your processing techniques are impeccable and I can''t state enough how much I appreciate the fact that you showed your original.  This is a truly perfect example of how you can process an image to convey your own personal vision.  Expertly accomplished and definitely worthy of the blue ribbon.  Congratulations!', '2008-06-09 23:46:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760775, 678362, 79955, '<td valign="top">Just saw your image. How did this score so low ? Deserves much higher.</td>', 'Just saw your image. How did this score so low ? Deserves much higher.', '2008-06-10 00:20:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760908, 678848, 49643, '<td valign="top">Congratulations for your success &amp; big thank you for sharing your very good post processing!</td>', 'Congratulations for your success & big thank you for sharing your very good post processing!', '2008-06-10 02:13:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760995, 678848, 34938, '<td valign="top">Amazing editing...20 :)</td>', 'Amazing editing...20 :)', '2008-06-10 04:42:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760998, 682153, 30214, '<td valign="top">excellent composition!</td>', 'excellent composition!', '2008-06-10 04:58:25.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4761027, 678848, 78455, '<td valign="top">bloody hell, I wish I hadn''t asked! Lol. Thanks for posting those steps, it just goes to show what a master you are in the digital darkroom! your portfolio is just wonderful.</td>', 'bloody hell, I wish I hadn''t asked! Lol. Thanks for posting those steps, it just goes to show what a master you are in the digital darkroom! your portfolio is just wonderful.', '2008-06-10 06:11:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4761314, 682301, 33769, '<td valign="top">this is a beautiful shot- the wings look translucent against the background and yet have their own sparkle and texture! :) :-D looking forward to seeing what your June study is! :)</td>', 'this is a beautiful shot- the wings look translucent against the background and yet have their own sparkle and texture! :) :-D looking forward to seeing what your June study is! :)', '2008-06-10 11:02:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4761691, 678848, 65319, '<td valign="top">I searched high...and I searched low...until at last I saw it...The silhouette of a tiny UFO reflected in the eye of the deer...WHEW!  To my great relief, I may now consider this remarkable and worthwhile Pièce de résistance of your portfolio...a masterpiece of ART...::winks::<br/> <br/>Congrats on your ribbon, Richard!  Well done!</td>', 'I searched high...and I searched low...until at last I saw it...The silhouette of a tiny UFO reflected in the eye of the deer...WHEW!  To my great relief, I may now consider this remarkable and worthwhile Pièce de résistance of your portfolio...a masterpiece of ART...::winks:: Congrats on your ribbon, Richard!  Well done!', '2008-06-10 16:05:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4761722, 680904, 68586, '<td valign="top">Very handsome Leopard - nice background colours.</td>', 'Very handsome Leopard - nice background colours.', '2008-06-10 16:20:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4761773, 681207, 45187, '<td valign="top">beautiful</td>', 'beautiful', '2008-06-10 16:44:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4761776, 683058, 81852, '<td valign="top">This really reminded me of Sally Mann''s work. Well done. Very cute little girl. Love the attitude on her face!</td>', 'This really reminded me of Sally Mann''s work. Well done. Very cute little girl. Love the attitude on her face!', '2008-06-10 16:44:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4761796, 678848, 28882, '<td valign="top">really nice work, the editing work is remarkable.  congratulations.</td>', 'really nice work, the editing work is remarkable.  congratulations.', '2008-06-10 16:59:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4761912, 683985, 58785, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=614717" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/773/120/614717.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/773/120/614717.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/773/120/614717.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Yeap... it wasn''t clean enough :P<br/> <br/>Very nice photo :D I mean yours of course :P</td>', '  Yeap... it wasn''t clean enough :P Very nice photo :D I mean yours of course :P', '2008-06-10 18:08:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4761969, 684246, 20608, '<td valign="top">FLT DUDS great shot dude.</td>', 'FLT DUDS great shot dude.', '2008-06-10 18:37:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4762002, 683058, 37961, '<td valign="top">Darling Devine. Great high contrast.</td>', 'Darling Devine. Great high contrast.', '2008-06-10 19:03:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4762077, 684247, 48228, '<td valign="top"><b>P I C T U R E  P E R F E C T.....</b> <br/> <br/>I am so very pleased for you receiving a ribbon for this awesome image. Perfect lighting, detail, composition, and a wonderful achievement as it is also a personal best score for you Darlene.<br/> <br/>I have just returned home from our trip to Melbourne, and so pleased to see that this fine image had ribboned in a "Free Study".<br/> <br/>I am so proud of you dear friend.</td>', 'P I C T U R E  P E R F E C T.....  I am so very pleased for you receiving a ribbon for this awesome image. Perfect lighting, detail, composition, and a wonderful achievement as it is also a personal best score for you Darlene. I have just returned home from our trip to Melbourne, and so pleased to see that this fine image had ribboned in a "Free Study". I am so proud of you dear friend.', '2008-06-10 20:05:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4762112, 678848, 42013, '<td valign="top">To pile on the well deserved platitudes... ;)  Your skill at rendering the finished product is incredible. To see your submission and your original side by side leaves me speechless. You had a nice starting point but the transformation is really something to see. Great work Richard! Can I send you a few of my rejects? ;P  Thanks for sharing.</td>', 'To pile on the well deserved platitudes... ;)  Your skill at rendering the finished product is incredible. To see your submission and your original side by side leaves me speechless. You had a nice starting point but the transformation is really something to see. Great work Richard! Can I send you a few of my rejects? ;P  Thanks for sharing.', '2008-06-10 20:33:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4762242, 684027, 10985, '<td valign="top">Fabulous, beautiful, fascinating, inspiring!<br/> <br/>Congratulations on your excellent position and extraordinary work. Keep it up!</td>', 'Fabulous, beautiful, fascinating, inspiring! Congratulations on your excellent position and extraordinary work. Keep it up!', '2008-06-10 22:20:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4762264, 680904, 65234, '<td valign="top">I do love the way those background colors complement the Leopard, and the very direct stare of a confident animal.  Looking at my scores I apparently gave you a 7, so I liked it when I voted on it, too!<br/> <br/>The right side of the image looks a bit misty, like you took the picture with a zoom through something in the foreground, or the light was shining just into that side of the lens.  Don''t mind it so much in the background but I''d try to fix it on the cat (maybe a little selective burning, increase in saturation and/or contrast on the overbright bits).  And I''d clone out that bright thing on the left side of the leopard''s cheek.  Then I''d give it a 9 ;-)</td>', 'I do love the way those background colors complement the Leopard, and the very direct stare of a confident animal.  Looking at my scores I apparently gave you a 7, so I liked it when I voted on it, too! The right side of the image looks a bit misty, like you took the picture with a zoom through something in the foreground, or the light was shining just into that side of the lens.  Don''t mind it so much in the background but I''d try to fix it on the cat (maybe a little selective burning, increase in saturation and/or contrast on the overbright bits).  And I''d clone out that bright thing on the left side of the leopard''s cheek.  Then I''d give it a 9 ;-)', '2008-06-10 22:31:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4762359, 682885, 65234, '<td valign="top">I see I gave you a 6, so I thought this was good.  Things I like/d:  composition, subject (a spider on a tire, not something I see every day), detail on the tire, lighting on the tire.  Things I think could be improved: I''d like more detail on the spider and have him better lit (looks a little blown out), maybe a tighter crop to put the spider even more off-center and make him a bigger part of the picture.  Obviously I didn''t agree with the majority of voters in terms of score, so maybe others can give you better insight into your final score.</td>', 'I see I gave you a 6, so I thought this was good.  Things I like/d:  composition, subject (a spider on a tire, not something I see every day), detail on the tire, lighting on the tire.  Things I think could be improved: I''d like more detail on the spider and have him better lit (looks a little blown out), maybe a tighter crop to put the spider even more off-center and make him a bigger part of the picture.  Obviously I didn''t agree with the majority of voters in terms of score, so maybe others can give you better insight into your final score.', '2008-06-10 23:22:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4762395, 679152, 37719, '<td valign="top">Wow!  You know, I was in this challenge for a charity purpose.  But I didn''t vote nor did I even look through the images.  Congrats on your finish - Top 20 in a Free Study!  Impressive!  I love the image.  Extremely well composed and extremely well balanced - color/neutral; sharp/not sharp.  Well done Jimmy!  You nailed it!  This is a ''print'' I want.<br/> <br/> <br/> <br/>Did I say WOW!  Straight to fav''s!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-10 22:43:59.</i></td>', 'Wow!  You know, I was in this challenge for a charity purpose.  But I didn''t vote nor did I even look through the images.  Congrats on your finish - Top 20 in a Free Study!  Impressive!  I love the image.  Extremely well composed and extremely well balanced - color/neutral; sharp/not sharp.  Well done Jimmy!  You nailed it!  This is a ''print'' I want.   Did I say WOW!  Straight to fav''s!', '2008-06-10 23:42:13.000000', '2008-06-10 23:43:59.000000', 0),
(4762693, 680940, 54645, '<td valign="top">The composition is almost intriguing, but the lack of overall contrast drags it down. There is nothing on the white end of the spectrum IMO. This leaves the overall photo flat. The flip side is there is not enough texture in your main subject, the foreground ties. I think this type of photo needs a few of CS3 B and W adjustment layers to get the most out of it. It''s actually a fairly interesting shot IMO, it grew on me. I would have given this version a 5, as it''s not a bad photograph, just needs a more practiced conversion. Keep working on it. I love BW, and I''ve been spending a lot of time on it the last few months.</td>', 'The composition is almost intriguing, but the lack of overall contrast drags it down. There is nothing on the white end of the spectrum IMO. This leaves the overall photo flat. The flip side is there is not enough texture in your main subject, the foreground ties. I think this type of photo needs a few of CS3 B and W adjustment layers to get the most out of it. It''s actually a fairly interesting shot IMO, it grew on me. I would have given this version a 5, as it''s not a bad photograph, just needs a more practiced conversion. Keep working on it. I love BW, and I''ve been spending a lot of time on it the last few months.', '2008-06-11 01:02:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4762916, 683058, 33361, '<td valign="top">WOW Judy.. this is fab!!!</td>', 'WOW Judy.. this is fab!!!', '2008-06-11 01:46:53.000000', NULL, 0),
