(4764107, 682648, 49804, '<td valign="top">Nailed composition here, really a very unique waterfall as well, one thing I might try would be bringing out the shadows in the water, to make it be just a little more defined, really a very nice shot though.</td>', 'Nailed composition here, really a very unique waterfall as well, one thing I might try would be bringing out the shadows in the water, to make it be just a little more defined, really a very nice shot though.', '2008-06-11 14:06:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4764165, 681065, 41794, '<td valign="top">I liked this shot because it was a different perspective from what is normally seen of Half Dome. I am guessing it may have fared a little better without the border.</td>', 'I liked this shot because it was a different perspective from what is normally seen of Half Dome. I am guessing it may have fared a little better without the border.', '2008-06-11 14:36:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4764187, 681065, 67152, '<td valign="top">I like one of the outtakes better than your entry.  The thing I noticed about the FS entry is an apparent cyan halo artifact around Half Dome and the mountains around it.  The outtakes don''t seem to have this artifact.<br/> <br/>Compositionally, all the shots are solid and provide an interesting and more unique view of one of the most famous rocks in the world.</td>', 'I like one of the outtakes better than your entry.  The thing I noticed about the FS entry is an apparent cyan halo artifact around Half Dome and the mountains around it.  The outtakes don''t seem to have this artifact. Compositionally, all the shots are solid and provide an interesting and more unique view of one of the most famous rocks in the world.', '2008-06-11 14:45:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4764356, 680030, 85097, '<td valign="top">I would have liked to see the man a little more in focus.  Its a great environmental portrait, but I think that the emphasis needs to be on the man, and it also seems like there is a little blur motion in his hand.<br/> <br/>If you had a speed light (that you can detach) you could have lit the man from the side (behind the figure he is working on) for a more dramatic effect.<br/> <br/>I think the composition is good because the shape of the figure leads right to the man so it draws your eye in.  <br/> <br/></td>', 'I would have liked to see the man a little more in focus.  Its a great environmental portrait, but I think that the emphasis needs to be on the man, and it also seems like there is a little blur motion in his hand. If you had a speed light (that you can detach) you could have lit the man from the side (behind the figure he is working on) for a more dramatic effect. I think the composition is good because the shape of the figure leads right to the man so it draws your eye in.   ', '2008-06-11 15:46:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4764372, 678848, 50034, '<td valign="top">Amazing Photo &amp; Post-Process!  Certainly a dead-on Blue Ribbon!  :)</td>', 'Amazing Photo & Post-Process!  Certainly a dead-on Blue Ribbon!  :)', '2008-06-11 15:50:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4764376, 678848, 65627, '<td valign="top">First off, I have to add my congratulations to a nice capture that made the rest of the editing possible, and to a wonderful job of Disney editing.  I just don''t see it as believable though, mostly because the contrast on the body of the front deer is not realistic (the whites are too bright).  My other regret is that you cleaned the highlights out of the ears.  That was highlighting the direction and intensity of the light, and couples with the highlights on the head of the deer to add quite a bit of depth, beauty, and believability to the rest of the image. <br/> <br/>All of that being said, I like the rest of your edits, and congratulate you on your blue! ..... and thanks for detailing your editing process!!!</td>', 'First off, I have to add my congratulations to a nice capture that made the rest of the editing possible, and to a wonderful job of Disney editing.  I just don''t see it as believable though, mostly because the contrast on the body of the front deer is not realistic (the whites are too bright).  My other regret is that you cleaned the highlights out of the ears.  That was highlighting the direction and intensity of the light, and couples with the highlights on the head of the deer to add quite a bit of depth, beauty, and believability to the rest of the image.  All of that being said, I like the rest of your edits, and congratulate you on your blue! ..... and thanks for detailing your editing process!!!', '2008-06-11 15:50:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4764395, 684247, 50034, '<td valign="top">Amazing Creation of a Pleasant Pheasant!  :}  Great Work!  :)</td>', 'Amazing Creation of a Pleasant Pheasant!  :}  Great Work!  :)', '2008-06-11 15:57:17.000000', NULL, 0),
